# Query Builder and Operations

## Query Builder Interface
1. Type-safe operations using Zod schemas
2. Support chainable methods
3. DynamoDB-specific optimizations

## Core Operations
1. Get Item
   ```typescript
   // Type-safe get operation
   const user = await UserEntity.get({
     pk: 'USER#123',
     sk: 'METADATA'
   });
   // user is typed as z.infer<typeof userSchema>
   ```

2. Put Item
   ```typescript
   // Type-safe put operation
   const result = await UserEntity.put({
     pk: 'USER#123',
     sk: 'METADATA',
     type: 'USER',
     name: 'John',
     email: 'john@example.com'
   });
   ```

3. Update Item
   ```typescript
   // Type-safe update operation
   const result = await UserEntity.update({
     key: {
       pk: 'USER#123',
       sk: 'METADATA'
     },
     set: {
       name: 'John Updated'
     },
     add: {
       age: 1
     },
     remove: ['oldField']
   });
   ```

4. Delete Item
   ```typescript
   // Type-safe delete operation
   const result = await UserEntity.delete({
     pk: 'USER#123',
     sk: 'METADATA'
   });
   ```

## Query Operations
1. Query with Key Conditions
   ```typescript
   // Type-safe query operation
   const orders = await OrderEntity.query({
     keyCondition: {
       pk: 'USER#123',
       sk: { beginsWith: 'ORDER#' }
     },
     filter: {
       status: 'PENDING'
     }
   });
   ```

2. Scan with Filters
   ```typescript
   // Type-safe scan operation
   const users = await UserEntity.scan({
     filter: {
       type: 'USER',
       age: { gt: 18 }
     }
   });
   ```

## Expression Support
1. Update Expressions
   ```typescript
   // Type-safe update with expressions
   const result = await UserEntity.update({
     key: {
       pk: 'USER#123',
       sk: 'METADATA'
     },
     set: {
       name: 'John',
       age: 30
     },
     add: {
       points: 10
     },
     remove: ['oldField'],
     condition: 'attribute_exists(pk)'
   });
   ```

2. Condition Expressions
   ```typescript
   // Type-safe put with conditions
   const result = await UserEntity.put({
     pk: 'USER#123',
     sk: 'METADATA',
     type: 'USER',
     name: 'John'
   }, {
     condition: 'attribute_not_exists(pk)'
   });
   ```

## Batch Operations
1. Batch Get
   ```typescript
   // Type-safe batch get
   const results = await UserEntity.batchGet([
     { pk: 'USER#1', sk: 'METADATA' },
     { pk: 'USER#2', sk: 'METADATA' }
   ]);
   ```

2. Batch Write
   ```typescript
   // Type-safe batch write
   const results = await UserEntity.batchWrite({
     put: [
       {
         pk: 'USER#1',
         sk: 'METADATA',
         type: 'USER',
         name: 'John'
       },
       {
         pk: 'USER#2',
         sk: 'METADATA',
         type: 'USER',
         name: 'Jane'
       }
     ],
     delete: [
       { pk: 'USER#3', sk: 'METADATA' }
     ]
   });
   ```

## Transactions
```typescript
// Type-safe transaction
const result = await db.transaction()
  .put(UserEntity, {
    pk: 'USER#123',
    sk: 'METADATA',
    type: 'USER',
    name: 'John'
  })
  .put(OrderEntity, {
    pk: 'USER#123',
    sk: 'ORDER#456',
    type: 'ORDER',
    orderId: '456',
    userId: '123',
    amount: 100
  })
  .commit();
```

## Error Handling
1. Schema Validation Errors
   ```typescript
   try {
     const result = await UserEntity.put({
       pk: 'USER#123',
       sk: 'METADATA',
       type: 'USER',
       email: 'invalid-email' // Will fail Zod validation
     });
   } catch (error) {
     if (error instanceof ZodError) {
       // Handle schema validation error
     }
   }
   ```

2. DynamoDB Errors
   ```typescript
   try {
     const result = await UserEntity.put(invalidData);
   } catch (error) {
     if (error instanceof ConditionalCheckFailedError) {
       // Handle conditional check failure
     } else if (error instanceof DynamoDBError) {
       // Handle other DynamoDB errors
     }
   }
   ```

## Type Safety
1. Schema Inference
   ```typescript
   // Infer types from schemas
   type User = z.infer<typeof userSchema>;
   type Order = z.infer<typeof orderSchema>;

   // Use in operations
   const user: User = {
     pk: 'USER#123',
     sk: 'METADATA',
     type: 'USER',
     name: 'John',
     email: 'john@example.com'
   };

   await UserEntity.put(user);
   ```

2. Operation Types
   ```typescript
   // Type-safe query parameters
   type QueryParams = {
     keyCondition: {
       pk: string;
       sk: { beginsWith: string } | string;
     };
     filter?: Record<string, any>;
   };

   const params: QueryParams = {
     keyCondition: {
       pk: 'USER#123',
       sk: { beginsWith: 'ORDER#' }
     }
   };

   const orders = await OrderEntity.query(params);
   ```

## Query Conditions
1. Support all DynamoDB comparison operators
2. Chain multiple conditions
3. Support for complex expressions

```typescript
const result = await db
  .select()
  .from(users)
  .where(
    and(
      eq(users.status, 'active'),
      gt(users.age, 18),
      beginsWith(users.email, 'test')
    )
  );
```

## Index Usage
1. Support for GSI and LSI
2. Automatic index selection
3. Manual index specification

```typescript
const result = await db
  .select()
  .from(users)
  .where(eq(users.email, 'test@example.com'))
  .index('email-index');
```
